# Files in the served asset tree that must NOT be uploaded as public static
# assets.
# Cloudflare warns that uploading the worker as an asset exposes server-side
# source. The _worker.js directory is the worker bundle entry, not an asset.
_worker.js

# The photo + asset pipeline used to sit at www/scripts and be ignored here.
# It is tools/photos now, outside the served tree entirely, so there is nothing
# at that path to ignore and a stale entry would silently exclude any future
# www/scripts from upload.

# The previous shipped versions of the content-hashed shell, kept only as
# dictionary inputs, USED TO SIT HERE and be ignored. They live at src/dict/
# now, outside the served tree, so there is nothing at this path to exclude.
# /ad/ (the deltas themselves) is deliberately NOT ignored: the worker
# fetches those through ASSETS to answer an Available-Dictionary request.

# Hand-authored Markdown twins for the Worker-rendered prose pages, whose text
# lives in template literals no build can read. Seven of them today: /around,
# /bot, /coffee, /lens, /security, /terminal, /whoareyou. They are authored in
# src/content/md/ and stage to this path, and tools/gen-md-twins.ts publishes
# each one AT ITS PAGE'S PATH (/bot.md), so shipping this directory as well
# would serve the same twin at a second URL.
md
